Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: wine-sg
Source: https://github.com/Stained-Glass-OS/wine-sg
Comment: This repository contains build machinery and patches only. The Wine
 source itself is fetched from https://dl.winehq.org at build time and is not
 redistributed here; the binary package therefore ships Wine's code, under
 Wine's licence, built from that source plus the patches listed below.
 .
 Every patch is listed individually with its own author, because they do not
 share one: some are ours, some are carried from Debian's wine packaging, and
 one is upstream Wine's own. Tracking that accurately is the point -- a blanket
 "everything here is ours" would be wrong about most of this directory.

Files: *
Copyright: 2026 David Hamner and the Stained Glass OS contributors
License: LGPL-2.1+
Comment: Build machinery -- build.sh, the Makefile, debian/, the WoW64 gate.
 LGPL-2.1+ to match the Wine source it builds, rather than the project's usual
 AGPL, so that nothing here can complicate the Wine tree it operates on.

Files: patches/sg/*
Copyright: 2026 David Hamner and the Stained Glass OS contributors
License: LGPL-2.1+
Comment: Our own Wine patches. LGPL-2.1+ because they are modifications of
 Wine. Not submitted upstream -- see ADR 0006 in the stained-glass repo.

Files: theme/dark.py
Copyright: 2026 David Hamner and the Stained Glass OS contributors
License: LGPL-2.1+
Comment: Generates light.msstyles' Dark colour scheme (0160) from the Light
 style's own rendered images and INI; nothing drawn by hand, no third-party
 artwork.

Files: patches/sg/0100-notepad-a-real-editor-tabs-syntax-colours-exact-encodings.patch
Copyright: 2026 David Hamner and the Stained Glass OS contributors
 1997-1998 Marcel Baur, 2002 Sylvain Petreolle, 2002 Andriy Palamarchuk
License: LGPL-2.1+
Comment: Replaces Wine's Notepad with our own editor; the files it keeps from
 Wine's (main.c, notepad.rc, notepad_res.h) keep their original notices.
 Written clean-room: no Microsoft code, and no third-party editor component.

Files: patches/sg/0143-wevtsvc-the-event-log-service-keeps-the-logs.patch
 patches/sg/0144-advapi32-the-event-log-functions-talk-to-the-event-log-service.patch
Copyright: 2026 David Hamner and the Stained Glass OS contributors
 2020 Dmitry Timoshkov (wevtsvc.c's service skeleton)
 1995 Sven Verdoolaege, 1998 Juergen Schmied, 2003 Mike Hearn (advapi32 eventlog.c)
License: LGPL-2.1+
Comment: The event log service and its advapi32 client; the files they change
 keep their original notices. Written from the documented API (EVENTLOGRECORD,
 the event log functions) and Wine's own conformance tests; the log file
 format and the pipe protocol are our own.

Files: patches/sg/0190-dxgi-swap-chains-for-composition.patch
 patches/sg/0191-dcomp-a-device-window-targets-and-visuals.patch
Copyright: 2026 David Hamner and the Stained Glass OS contributors
License: LGPL-2.1+
Comment: DirectComposition's version-1 device and DXGI composition swap
 chains, enough for WebView2's GPU process. Written from the documented API;
 the interface layout from Wine's own headers and mingw-w64's public dcomp.h;
 how Chromium calls it from Chromium's BSD-licensed source. No Microsoft code.

Files: patches/sg/0340-d2d1-layers-primitive-blends-and-composite-modes.patch
 patches/sg/0341-d2d1-effect-graphs-shared-inputs-draw-info-image-rect.patch
 patches/sg/0342-win32u-dxgi-an-8-bit-srgb-sdr-display.patch
Copyright: 2026 David Hamner and the Stained Glass OS contributors
License: LGPL-2.1+
Comment: Direct2D layers, blend and composite modes, effect graph fixes, and a
 display's colour capabilities. Written from the documented APIs.

Files: patches/sg/0229-d2d1-draw-effects-and-command-lists.patch
 patches/sg/0231-dcomp-windows-ui-composition.patch
Copyright: 2026 David Hamner and the Stained Glass OS contributors
License: LGPL-2.1+
Comment: Direct2D effect rendering and a first Windows.UI.Composition. Written
 from the documented APIs; interface layouts from Wine's own IDL, IIDs and
 WinRT interface shapes checked against the MIT-licensed windows-rs crate's
 public metadata. The files they change keep their original notices. No
 Microsoft code, disassembly or symbols.

Files: patches/fixes/binutils2.44.patch
Copyright: the Wine project and the Debian wine packaging team
License: LGPL-2.1+
Comment: Carried unmodified from Debian's wine packaging. Fixes a crash when
 building with binutils-mingw-w64 2.44.
 WineHQ bug 57819; Debian bug 1101977.

Files: patches/fixes/virtual-protect.patch
Copyright: Fabian Maurer
License: LGPL-2.1+
Comment: Carried unmodified from Debian's wine packaging. Fixes incorrect
 handling of WRITECOPY memory protection.
 WineHQ bugs 29384 and 56711.

Files: patches/fixes/ntdll-398da925.patch
Copyright: Alexandre Julliard <julliard@winehq.org>
License: LGPL-2.1+
Comment: Carried unmodified from Debian's wine packaging; authored by Wine's
 maintainer.

Files: patches/fixes/fstype.patch
Copyright: Michael Gilbert <mgilbert@debian.org>
License: LGPL-2.1+
Comment: Carried unmodified from Debian's wine packaging.

